-- check/bad: a `Task.callback` canceller that may suspend
-- (transparent-effects-proposal.md §17.1 item 3, §15.2 item 1). The
-- runtime calls a wait's canceller synchronously, during cancellation, so
-- `callback`'s signature in core marks the returned canceller `sync` as well
-- as the registration. The registration is `sync_boundary`, and the chain
-- names `Task.yieldNow`.
import Task


pub bad : ⊤ → Int
bad ⊤ = Task.callback λ_ → λ⊤ → Task.yieldNow ⊤
